---
description: User flow and state transitions for the headshot generation process
globs: src/app/app/**/*.tsx, src/components/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---
- **User Flow Stages**
  - Each stage corresponds to specific routes and components
  - Flow enforces sequential progression through required steps
  - State management tracks completion of each stage

  ```typescript
  // Stage status types
  type FlowStage = 
    | 'shoot'         // Creating styles
    | 'payment'       // Payment processing
    | 'upload'        // Uploading user photos
    | 'review'        // Image quality review
    | 'shoots'        // Results viewing
  ```

- **1. Authentication (Route: /auth)**
  - Required before accessing any app features
  - Handled by Supabase authentication
  - Redirects to shoot page on success
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Check auth state before rendering protected routes
  if (!user) return <RedirectToAuth />
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Allow access to protected routes without auth
  if (!user) renderProtectedContent() // Wrong
  ```

- **2. Profile Check (Route: /app/settings/profile)**
  - Required before accessing any app features
  - If user has gender = null, redirects to profile settings
  - Must complete profile before accessing other pages
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Check profile completion
  if (!user.gender) return <RedirectToProfile />
  ```

- **3. Styles Page (Route: /app/shoot)**
  - Initial state shows empty grid with "New Style" button
  - Lists all draft styles for the user
  - "Next" button enabled only with at least one style
  - Can navigate to style creation page
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Filter styles by status
  .eq('status', 'draft')
  
  // ✅ DO: Enable next button conditionally
  disabled={styles.length === 0}
  ```

- **4. Style Creation (Route: /app/style)**
  - Three main selectors:
    - Photography Style (studio, natural, dramatic)
    - Outfit (professional, casual, creative)
    - Background (plain, office, outdoor, custom)
  - Can save or go back to shoot page
  - Saves as draft status
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Save with draft status
  status: 'draft' as StyleStatus
  
  // ✅ DO: Format name consistently
  `${photographyStyle} ${outfit} ${background}`
  ```

- **5. Payment (Route: /app/payment)**
  - Only accessible with at least one style
  - Shows order summary with selected styles
  - Can go back to shoot or style pages
  - Handles payment processing
  - Updates style status on successful payment
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Update all styles on payment
  styles.map(style => updateStatus(style.id, 'processing'))
  
  // ✅ DO: Show clear payment feedback
  paymentStatus, paymentError
  ```

- **6. Payment Success (Route: /app/payment/success)**
  - Only accessible after successful payment
  - Shows success message
  - Provides button to proceed to upload
  - Cannot go back to previous stages

- **7. Photo Upload (Route: /app/upload)**
  - Only accessible after successful payment
  - Cannot go back to previous stages
  - Handles multiple photo uploads
  - Validates image requirements:
    - Minimum resolution
    - Face detection
    - Image quality checks
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Validate images before upload
  validateImageRequirements(file)
  
  // ✅ DO: Show clear upload feedback
  uploadProgress, uploadStatus
  ```

- **8. Upload Review (Route: /app/review)**
  - Shows upload results with quality ratings
  - Can go back to upload page only
  - Allows re-upload of rejected images
  - Requires all images to pass quality check
  - Provides button to start AI generation
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Show clear rejection reasons
  image.rejectionReasons.map(reason => ...)
  
  // ✅ DO: Enable continue only when all images valid
  disabled={hasRejectedImages}
  ```

- **9. My Shoots (Route: /app/shoots)**
  - Shows all compositions grouped by status:
    - Completed: Ready for viewing
    - Processing: Being generated
    - Draft: Not yet submitted
  - Cannot go back to any previous stages
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Group compositions by status
  groupBy(compositions, 'status')
  
  // ✅ DO: Sort by creation date within groups
  orderBy(group, 'created_at', 'desc')
  ```

- **State Transitions**
  ```mermaid
  graph LR
    A[Draft] --> B[Processing]
    B --> C[Completed]
    B --> D[Failed]
    D --> A
  ```

- **Error Handling**
  - Each stage should handle:
    - Network errors
    - Validation failures
    - Payment failures
    - Processing errors
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Show user-friendly error messages
  toast({
    title: 'Error',
    description: getErrorMessage(error),
    variant: 'destructive'
  })
  ```

- **Navigation Rules**
  - Forward progression requires completion of previous steps
  - Back navigation allowed to any previous step
  - Composition editing only allowed in draft status
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Check step completion
  if (!hasCompletedPrp) redirect('/previous-step')
  
  //nly in draft
  disabled={compos}
  ```

